{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-216592","model_call":21,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"reasons\" (+ buy need) \"income\")"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"reasons\" (+ buy need) \"income\")"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_864673331#8_1759791403","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1178","rank":1,"snippet":"Retirement Other Reasons to Buy a Disability Policy Consider Long-Term Disability As You Approach Retirement Do I Need Long-Term Disability Insurance? Do I have enough saved so that I can retire in comfort today? \" , \"segment\": \"She needs to protect that income via a long-term term disability policy. She also can’t afford to tap her limited savings prematurely – which she would have to do to support herself in the absence of <cover>income (as the result of a long-term disability). Therefore, a long-term disability policy is a must-have for this client. Other Reasons to Buy a Disability Policy So far, we’ve covered the feasibility of purchasing disability insurance </cover>in two different scenarios: Where someone has saved a lot, and therefore probably doesn’t need long-term disability insurance. Where someone’s savings are inadequate, and therefore very likely needs long-term disability insurance. There’s one more category we haven’t yet covered: where a household has a large nest egg and a huge appetite for spending. Recently, we worked with an engineer who received a large windfall. Outside of this windfall, this gentlemen had very limited savings."},"time":875},"model_calls":21,"document_judgments":18,"relevance_3":14,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
