{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-216592","model_call":30,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1181"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1181"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_563507936#7_1149049181","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1181","rank":3,"snippet":"your expenses while still protecting your future. There isn’t much bad to say about an SIS rider. Everyone likes to save money, and everyone likes to protect their future to the greatest extent possible. This type of disability insurance policy allows you to accomplish both of those goals. Whether or not you choose to save money with a Social Insurance Supplement Rider It all boils down to this… You only have three options to choose from when the unexpected accident or <cover>illness happens, and your payroll deposit stops: You can deplete your savings and retirement accounts You have a wealthy family member that will pay bills for you You planned ahead and have a disability insurance </cover>policy in place that delivers monthly, tax-free cash to your bank account, until you are ready to go back to work Are you ready to speak with your own disability insurance coach? Click here or call today!\" , \"start_char\": 4152.000000 , \"title\": \"What is a Social Insurance Substitute Rider or SIS Rider? – Disability Insurance Coach\" , \"url\": \"https://disabilityinsurancecoach.com/riders/what-is-a-social-"},"time":8},"model_calls":30,"document_judgments":27,"relevance_3":21,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
