{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-216592","model_call":51,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":24229,"output_tokens":247,"total_tokens":24476,"cached_tokens":20224,"reasoning_tokens":67},"output_characters":905,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_2062771509#6_3383748471","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to short-term versus long-term disability insurance and directly explains why coverage is financially smart: if emergency savings cannot cover expenses during a period unable to work, short-term disability is essential financial protection, while long-term disability protects financial wellbeing and retirement plans against permanent disability.","learned":"Disability insurance is a smart investment because it fills gaps that emergency savings may not cover and protects both immediate expenses and long-term retirement/financial wellbeing if disability prevents work."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1192","reason":"Continue this focused query because it is producing dedicated disability insurance guidance with direct evidence about covering expenses when unable to work."}}}
